ode4.irmos2:
O Lord, I have heard the mystery of Thy dispensation;
I have considered Thy works,
and I have glorified Thy Divinity.

ode6.irmos2:
Cleanse me, O Savior,
for many are mine iniquities;
lead me up from the abyss of evils I pray Thee,
for unto Thee have I cried,
and Thou hast hearkened unto me,
O God of my salvation.

ode9.irmos:
O Isaiah, rejoice and be glad!
The Virgin hath conceived in her womb,
and hath borne a Son, Emmanuel,
who is both God and man;
and Orient is His name;
Him we magnify, and the Virgin we call blessed.
